CloudBurrow patch 18 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1370). Applies after patch 0016; needs
googlesqlite patch 0030.

Every table made by tables.insert is made in the engine with the
pseudo-column _PARTITION_STREAMED TIMESTAMP, the time a row was streamed
(googlesqlite patch 0030), and a CREATE TABLE's schema leaves the column
out as it leaves out _PARTITIONTIME. CloudBurrow's front sets it on the
rows tabledata.insertAll streams, and refuses DML that would change one
streamed in the last 30 minutes, as BigQuery does
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/data-manipulation-language).

